    "state": "APPROVED",
    "body": "Verified the two claims this turns on, both hold.\n\n**Pro shadowing.** `tryRegister`'s `try` covers the `fn(program)` call, not just the `import` (`Ix-pro/src/cli/register.ts:17-23`), so commander's duplicate-name throw is swallowed. `main.ts:69` runs `registerOssCommands` synchronously before the Pro probe at :74, so the OSS registration is the survivor. And `Ix-pro/src/cli/commands/patches.ts` is now identical to this one bar the `llm` in its `--format` description — it already imports `createClient` and `formatPatches` from `@ix/cli`, so switching to `createClient()` here makes them the same call, not merely a similar one.\n\n**One gap, fixed in 89ca55e.** The new test pins that `patches` is absent from the stub list. That is the half that can't silently regress — the other half can. I deleted the `registerPatchesCommand(program)` line from `oss.ts` and the whole suite stayed green (722 passed) while `ix patches` went back to being commander's `unknown command`, i.e. the state #371 was filed about.\n\nAdded `registers patches as an OSS command` alongside it, asserting the command exists on the program after `registerOssCommands` and carries `--format`. It fails with `expected undefined to be defined` against that mutation.\n\nBoth halves are now pinned. 723 green.",
